# No browser dialogs in popup UI

Never use `window.alert`, `window.confirm`, `window.prompt`, or bare `alert()` / `confirm()` / `prompt()` in popup React code. Native dialogs block the UI thread, ignore theme tokens, and break extension UX.

## Use the modal system

1. Wrap app roots with `ModalProvider` (already in `main.jsx` and `dashboard-main.jsx`).
2. In components, call `useModal()`:

```jsx
import { useModal } from "../hooks/useModal.js";

const { showAlert, showConfirm, showPrompt } = useModal();

await showAlert("Saved.", { title: "Success", variant: "success" });
const ok = await showConfirm("Discard changes?", { variant: "warning" });
const url = await showPrompt({ title: "Link URL", defaultValue: "https://" });
```

Variants: `info` | `success` | `error` | `warning`.

## Custom or large content

Use `Modal` from `components/Modal.jsx` with local `open` state (see `ReviewPanel` CV preview, `CvTemplateRichEditor` link URL).

```jsx
import { Modal, ModalButton } from "./Modal.jsx";

<Modal open={open} onClose={() => setOpen(false)} title="Title" size="lg" footer={...}>
  {children}
</Modal>
```

## Adding new entry points

Any new popup bundle (`main.jsx`, `dashboard-main.jsx`, etc.) must include `<ModalProvider>` inside `ThemeProvider`.
